<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dawda Jawara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1924–2019</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dawda Jawara was a Gambian veterinarian and politician who led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-gambia">The Gambia</a> to independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1965. His People's Progressive Party won the elections of 1962, making him head of government, and he became president when the country became a republic in 1970. He governed until 1994, when he was overthrown in a military coup led by Yahya Jammeh.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dawda-jawara.jpg" alt="Dawda Jawara" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fernando Pereira / Anefo · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dawda_Jawara_(1979).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
